codemap 8
path lsp-client
kind layer
author ai
group index
note A minimal language-server client: JSON-RPC over the spawned server's stdio, and nothing more of the protocol than this tool needs. Requests are synchronous - a reader thread queues every incoming message and request() blocks for the matching id, servicing notifications and the server's own requests as they go by, which is what keeps a chatty server from deadlocking. The client is used by the index's server backend (index/server.rs) for exactly three things: document symbols, outgoing calls and references. Everything about it is shaped by one fact: a server takes seconds to become useful, so wait_ready exists and the answers are cached.

